Write a console-based Java application for a Library to manage book and member details.

Requirements:

There are two types of members in the library:

Student Member

Faculty Member

Each member (student or faculty) has the following details:

Name

Date of Membership (use LocalDate)

Phone Number

Aadhaar Number

Additional fields:

For Student Member → courseName and yearOfStudy

For Faculty Member → departmentName and designation

Book Details:

Each book has the following fields:

bookId (auto-generated, unique)

title

author

price

isAvailable (boolean)

Rules & Validations:

memberId and bookId should be auto-generated and unique.

Phone number must be numeric and exactly 10 digits (^[0-9]{10}$).

Aadhaar number must be numeric and exactly 12 digits (^[0-9]{12}$), and must be unique (no two members share same Aadhaar).

Date of membership must be a valid LocalDate.

Books can be issued only if available.

When a book is issued, mark it as not available.

When returned, mark it as available again.

Operations Menu:

1️⃣ Add a Student Member
2️⃣ Add a Faculty Member
3️⃣ Add a Book
4️⃣ Issue a Book to Member (by Book ID and Member ID)
5️⃣ Return a Book (by Book ID)
6️⃣ Delete a Member by Member ID
7️⃣ Search a Member by Aadhaar number
8️⃣ Display all Members
9️⃣ Display all Books (sorted by title)
🔟 Exit